compemu_support: a guest cache flush revalidates only the translations it can have changed

flush_icache_range(start, size), which the BlockMove and FlushInstructionCache
traps reach through FlushCodeCache(), threw its range away and called the
whole-cache flush. Under lazy invalidation that sends every active block back
to "needs checking", so each of the hundreds of flushes a second System 7.6.1
asks for makes the next entry of every hot block recompute its checksum — on a
Raspberry Pi 4, half of the dispatcher's entries after the escalation fix are
check_checksum calls.

The range is exact and the blocks carry their source spans, so only the blocks
whose spans overlap it go back to "needs checking" and onto the dormant list,
the same marking flush_icache_lazy() gives all of them. Blocks without spans
(ROM) and blocks elsewhere stay active. The hard policy is unchanged, and the
line and page forms of CINV and CPUSH (scope bits 4:3 = 01, 10), which the
68040 Mac OS executes with every BlockMove, take the same path with their
(An) range; CINVA/CPUSHA still flush everything. Counted under QEMU, boot of
System 7.1: about 8,500 whole-cache flushes in 13 s, each marking about 118
active blocks, next to 8,000 FlushCodeCache() calls of 670 bytes on average.

Only in a: .git
diff --git a/BasiliskII/src/uae_cpu_2026/compiler/compemu_support.cpp b/BasiliskII/src/uae_cpu_2026/compiler/compemu_support.cpp
